<section id="S6" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">6 </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="S6.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Existing literature on Fairness in T2I methods</h3>

<div id="S6.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Prior work on fair T2I mostly falls into three camps: adding semantic guidance during diffusion optimization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dewan et al. 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib47" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shen et al. 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Jung et al. 2025</a>)</cite>, injecting debiasing embeddings into the latent space <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al. 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Azam and Akhtar 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. 2025c</a>)</cite>,, or applying classifier-guided noise control<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">Brack et al. 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kim et al. 2025</a>)</cite>. Lightweight alternatives modify attention maps <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gandikota et al. 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib52" title="" class="ltx_ref">Teo et al. 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib61" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhou et al. 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib41" title="" class="ltx_ref">Park et al. 2025</a>)</cite> or adjust the bottleneck representations in the U-Net <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. 2024a</a>; <a href="#bib.bib48" title="" class="ltx_ref">Shi et al. 2025</a>)</cite>, avoiding full model retraining.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SSx2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Implementation Details</h3>

<div id="S6.SSx2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SSx2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SSx2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">VE Evaluation Metrics</span> To demonstrate that our model effectively preserves VE capabilities, we adopt a suite of established CLIP similarity metrics <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Radford et al. 2021</a>)</cite> that capture both edit fidelity and temporal consistency. We primarily focus on CLIP-based metrics to measure semantic alignment and structural coherence. Specifically, we employ CLIP-T, which calculates the average cosine similarity between the input text prompt and all generated video frames using CLIP embeddings, thereby reflecting how well the output video aligns with the intended prompt semantics. CLIP-F measures the average cosine similarity between consecutive video frames, serving as an indicator of temporal coherence within the generated sequence. TIFA score evaluates semantic alignment between the target image and the edited video frames. Additionally, Warp-Err quantifies the pixel-level deviation by warping each edited frame based on the optical flow of the source video using <span id="S6.SSx2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">RAFT-Large</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib51" title="" class="ltx_ref">Teed and Deng 2020</a>)</cite>, thereby evaluating motion consistency.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SSx2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SSx2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SSx2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Experimental Settings</span> We build our framework upon SD 1.5<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
              
              
              
              
              
              
            https://huggingface.co/stable-diffusion-v1-5/stable-diffusion-v1-5</span></span></span>, utilizing its released pre-trained weights along with the DDIM scheduler <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib50" title="" class="ltx_ref">Song, Meng, and Ermon 2021</a>)</cite> with 50 steps for inverse to acquarie attention maps. Each video–text pair is represented as the tuple (source video, instruction, SAM masks, ControlNet annotators). We employ SAM-tracking <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cheng et al. 2023</a>)</cite> based masks to perform object-level clustering, enabling fine-grained edge segmentation. To support controllable image-level editing, we integrate several ControlNet annotators <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib59" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang, Rao, and Agrawala 2023</a>)</cite>, including DW-Pose, Depth-Zoe, Depth-MiDaS, and OpenPose (totaling approximately 4 GB). We retain the default <span id="S6.SSx2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">guidance_scale</span> parameter to control the influence of the prompt on the editing outcome. Additionally, we enable Prompt-to-Prompt (PnP) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hertz et al. 2023</a>)</cite> editing to modulate spatial or semantic regions across frames. All experiments are conducted on a single NVIDIA Tesla H100 GPU.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S6.SSx3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection">Additional Results</h3>

<div id="S6.SSx3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SSx3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S6.F4" title="In Additional Results ‣ 6 Appendix ‣ FAME: Fairness-aware Attention-modulated Video Editing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> verify the necessity of the importance of balanced modulation strength for fairness-aware prompt design in T2I based training-free VE models.</p>
</div>
<div id="S6.SSx3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SSx3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><a href="#S6.F5" title="In Additional Results ‣ 6 Appendix ‣ FAME: Fairness-aware Attention-modulated Video Editing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> shows the full test pipeline and results for the Prompt Responsiveness Test mentioned in <a href="#S3.SSx1" title="Prompt Responsiveness Test for Fairness Verification in Video Editing ‣ 3 Methodology ‣ FAME: Fairness-aware Attention-modulated Video Editing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Section</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S6.F4" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.22960v1/prompt.png" id="S6.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:698/768;" width="698" height="768" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 4: </span>Comparison of different prompt injection methods. Direct addition leads to semantic confusion, while our masked fusion retains structure and enhances fairness controllability.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="S6.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.22960v1/prompt-test.png" id="S6.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:698/618;" width="698" height="618" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 5: </span>
<span id="S6.F5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt Responsiveness Test.</span> We evaluate three training-free VE models, including FateZero, TokenFlow, and VideoGrain, on a single example <math id="S6.F5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext='{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{P}}}_{\texttt{ref}}=\texttt{"A man is playing tennis"}' display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">ref</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">"A man is playing tennis"</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{P}}}_{\texttt{ref}}=\texttt{"A man is playing tennis"}</annotation></semantics></math> to assess their responsiveness to debiasing prompt. The top row shows the input reference frames. Rows 2–4 display results using different prompts on several baselines, including FateZero <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib42" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qi et al. 2023</a>)</cite>, TokenFlow <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Geyer et al. 2024</a>)</cite>, and VideoGrain <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib56" title="" class="ltx_ref">Yang et al. 2025</a>)</cite>, while the 5th row shows the results with the original editing prompt <math id="S6.F5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext='{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{P}}}_{\texttt{tar}}=\texttt{"A teacher is playing tennis"}' display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">tar</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">"A teacher is playing tennis"</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{P}}}_{\texttt{tar}}=\texttt{"A teacher is playing tennis"}</annotation></semantics></math> by our FAME. In rows 2–4, the left column shows the editing performance with the original prompt, and the right column shows the editing performance guided by the directly injected prompt <math id="S6.F5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext='{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{P}}}_{\texttt{tar}}=\texttt{"A male teacher is playing tennis"}' display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐏</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">tar</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">"A male teacher is playing tennis"</mtext></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{P}}}_{\texttt{tar}}=\texttt{"A male teacher is playing tennis"}</annotation></semantics></math> as the debiasing prompt. In the last row, our FAME can generate the female version (left column) and the debiased male content (right column). In the 2nd and 3rd rows, FateZero and TokenFlow exhibit a mismatch between the debiasing prompt and the visual semantics, indicating degraded video fidelity. In the 4th row, VideoGrain shows that directly injecting debiasing prompts often leads to semantic degradation in generated frames. This suggests that fairness-sensitive prompts may disrupt the alignment between the prompt and visual output. In the last row, our FAME can generate different gender-profession content even with the original prompt.
</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S6.SSx3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S6.SSx3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S6.SSx3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pseudo Algorithm Code.</span>
Our full inference procedure is composed of three core modules, shown in <a href="#alg1" title="In Additional Results ‣ 6 Appendix ‣ FAME: Fairness-aware Attention-modulated Video Editing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>,<a href="#alg2" title="In Additional Results ‣ 6 Appendix ‣ FAME: Fairness-aware Attention-modulated Video Editing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> and <a href="#alg3" title="In Additional Results ‣ 6 Appendix ‣ FAME: Fairness-aware Attention-modulated Video Editing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. <a href="#alg1" title="In Additional Results ‣ 6 Appendix ‣ FAME: Fairness-aware Attention-modulated Video Editing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> describes the fairness-aware text embedding procedure, which softly fuses debiasing attribute tokens into the original prompt embedding to retain semantic structure while introducing fairness control. <a href="#alg2" title="In Additional Results ‣ 6 Appendix ‣ FAME: Fairness-aware Attention-modulated Video Editing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> defines the fairness-aware self-attention modulation that enhances intra-region coherence by amplifying attention within fairness-relevant areas and suppressing unrelated interactions. <a href="#alg3" title="In Additional Results ‣ 6 Appendix ‣ FAME: Fairness-aware Attention-modulated Video Editing" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Algorithm</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> introduces the fairness-aware cross-attention mechanism, where alignment between prompt tokens and visual regions is refined using a similarity-based attention mask.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Soft Debiasing Prompt Encoding via Position-Aware Fusion</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.3" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
             Target prompt <math id="alg1.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{p}}}_{\texttt{tar}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">tar</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{p}}}_{\texttt{tar}}</annotation></semantics></math>, fairness prompt <math id="alg1.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{p}}}_{\texttt{fair}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">fair</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{p}}}_{\texttt{fair}}</annotation></semantics></math>, pre-trained text encoder <math id="alg1.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{\phi}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{\phi}}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l0a" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
             Debiased embedding matrix <math id="alg1.l0a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{e}}}}\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{e}}}}\in\mathbb{R}^{L\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
             <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{e}}}_{\texttt{tar}}\leftarrow{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{\phi}}}({\boldsymbol{\mathbf{p}}}_{\texttt{tar}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">tar</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">tar</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{e}}}_{\texttt{tar}}\leftarrow{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{\phi}}}({\boldsymbol{\mathbf{p}}}_{\texttt{tar}})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;">// Token embeddings of target prompt
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
             <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{e}}}_{\texttt{fair}}\leftarrow{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{\phi}}}({\boldsymbol{\mathbf{p}}}_{\texttt{fair}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">fair</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_bold-italic" mathvariant="bold-italic">ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐩</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">fair</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{e}}}_{\texttt{fair}}\leftarrow{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{\phi}}}({\boldsymbol{\mathbf{p}}}_{\texttt{fair}})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;">// Token embeddings of fairness prompt
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
             <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}\leftarrow\textsc{GenerateSoftMask}({\boldsymbol{\mathbf{e}}}_{\texttt{tar}},{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{e}}}_{\texttt{fair}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">GenerateSoftMask</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">tar</mtext></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">fair</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}\leftarrow\textsc{GenerateSoftMask}({\boldsymbol{\mathbf{e}}}_{\texttt{tar}},{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{e}}}_{\texttt{fair}})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;">// Soft mask: <math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{M}\in[0,1]^{L\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{M}\in[0,1]^{L\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
             <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{e}}}}\leftarrow{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{e}}}_{\texttt{tar}}+\mathbf{M}\otimes({\boldsymbol{\mathbf{e}}}_{\texttt{fair}}-{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{e}}}_{\texttt{tar}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">tar</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝐌</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">fair</mtext></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">tar</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{e}}}}\leftarrow{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{e}}}_{\texttt{tar}}+\mathbf{M}\otimes({\boldsymbol{\mathbf{e}}}_{\texttt{fair}}-{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{e}}}_{\texttt{tar}})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;">// Soft injection
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
             <span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{e}}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐞</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{e}}}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Self-attention Manipulation</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.3" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
             Latent tensor <math id="alg2.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{z}}}_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times w\times\ell\times c}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{z}}}_{t}\in\mathbb{R}^{h\times w\times\ell\times c}</annotation></semantics></math>, projections <math id="alg2.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{Q}}},W_{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{K}}},W_{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>𝐊</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>𝐕</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{Q}}},W_{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{K}}},W_{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, coefficients <math id="alg2.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg2.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{\mu}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝝁</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{\mu}}}</annotation></semantics></math>, temperature <math id="alg2.l0.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l0a" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
             Attention output <math id="alg2.l0a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{A}}}\in\mathbb{R}^{(h\cdot w)\times\ell\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{A}}}\in\mathbb{R}^{(h\cdot w)\times\ell\times d}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
             <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{z}}}^{\prime}\leftarrow\varphi({\boldsymbol{\mathbf{z}}}_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>φ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{z}}}^{\prime}\leftarrow\varphi({\boldsymbol{\mathbf{z}}}_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;">// Flatten spatial dims to <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(h\cdot w)\times\ell\times c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(h\cdot w)\times\ell\times c</annotation></semantics></math>
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
             <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{Q}}},{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{K}}},{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{V}}}\leftarrow W_{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{Q}}}{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{z}}}^{\prime},\ W_{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{K}}}{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{z}}}^{\prime},\ W_{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{V}}}{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{z}}}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝐕</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>𝐐</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>𝐊</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>W</mi><mi>𝐕</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐳</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{Q}}},{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{K}}},{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{V}}}\leftarrow W_{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{Q}}}{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{z}}}^{\prime},\ W_{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{K}}}{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{z}}}^{\prime},\ W_{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{V}}}{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{z}}}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;">// Project to attention space
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
             <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{\text{raw}}\leftarrow{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{Q}}}{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{K}}}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mtext>raw</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msup><mi>𝐐𝐊</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{\text{raw}}\leftarrow{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{Q}}}{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{K}}}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;">// Raw attention scores
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
             Compute <math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{M}}}^{\text{pos}},{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{M}}}^{\text{neg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mtext>pos</mtext></msup><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mtext>neg</mtext></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{M}}}^{\text{pos}},{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{M}}}^{\text{neg}}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="alg2.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{\text{raw}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mtext>raw</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{\text{raw}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
             Compute region mask <math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{R}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐑</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{R}}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;">// 1 if same region, else 0
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
             <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{M}}}^{\text{fair}}\leftarrow{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{R}}}\odot{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{M}}}^{\text{pos}}-(1-{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{R}}})\odot{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{M}}}^{\text{neg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mtext>fair</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐑</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mtext>pos</mtext></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐑</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mtext>neg</mtext></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{M}}}^{\text{fair}}\leftarrow{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{R}}}\odot{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{M}}}^{\text{pos}}-(1-{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{R}}})\odot{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{M}}}^{\text{neg}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
             Compute per-position feature mean: <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{f}_{\texttt{q}}=\frac{1}{\ell}\sum_{t=1}^{\ell}{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{z}}}_{t}[\texttt{q}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">q</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>𝐳</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">q</mtext><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{f}_{\texttt{q}}=\frac{1}{\ell}\sum_{t=1}^{\ell}{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{z}}}_{t}[\texttt{q}]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
             Compute similarity mask: <math id="alg2.l8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{S}}}[\texttt{q}_{1},\texttt{q}_{2}]=\exp(-\|\mathbf{f}_{\texttt{q}_{1}}-\mathbf{f}_{\texttt{q}_{2}}\|^{2}/\tau^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐒</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">q</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">q</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">q</mtext><mn>1</mn></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐟</mi><msub><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">q</mtext><mn>2</mn></msub></msub><msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><msup><mi>τ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{S}}}[\texttt{q}_{1},\texttt{q}_{2}]=\exp(-\|\mathbf{f}_{\texttt{q}_{1}}-\mathbf{f}_{\texttt{q}_{2}}\|^{2}/\tau^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
             <math id="alg2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g({\boldsymbol{\mathbf{Q}}},{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{K}}})\leftarrow(\mathbf{A}_{\text{raw}}+\lambda{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{M}}}^{\text{fair}}+{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{\mu}}}{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{S}}})/\sqrt{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mtext>raw</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐌</mi><mtext>fair</mtext></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>𝝁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐒</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>d</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g({\boldsymbol{\mathbf{Q}}},{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{K}}})\leftarrow(\mathbf{A}_{\text{raw}}+\lambda{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{M}}}^{\text{fair}}+{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{\mu}}}{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{S}}})/\sqrt{d}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
             <math id="alg2.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{A}}}\leftarrow\text{softmax}(g({\boldsymbol{\mathbf{Q}}},{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{K}}}))\cdot{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{V}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐐</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐊</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>𝐕</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{A}}}\leftarrow\text{softmax}(g({\boldsymbol{\mathbf{Q}}},{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{K}}}))\cdot{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{V}}}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg2.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;">// Final output
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg2.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
              
             <span id="alg2.l11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  <math id="alg2.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{A}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐀</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{A}}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg3" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span> Cross-attention Reweighting</figcaption>
<div id="alg3.3" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg3.l0" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
             <math id="alg3.l0.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{Q}}}_{t},{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{K}}}_{t},{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{V}}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐕</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{Q}}}_{t},{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{K}}}_{t},{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{V}}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, fairness token set <math id="alg3.l0.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{e}}}_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{e}}}_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, token groups <math id="alg3.l0.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\tau_{k}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\tau_{k}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, coefficient <math id="alg3.l0.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l0a" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">0:</span>
              
             Cross-attention output <math id="alg3.l0a.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{A}}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{A}}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
             <math id="alg3.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{\text{raw}}\leftarrow{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{Q}}}_{t}{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{K}}}_{t}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mtext>raw</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐊</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{\text{raw}}\leftarrow{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{Q}}}_{t}{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{K}}}_{t}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;">// Raw attention matrix
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
             Compute <math id="alg3.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{M}}}_{t}^{\text{pos}},{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{M}}}_{t}^{\text{neg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>pos</mtext></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>neg</mtext></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{M}}}_{t}^{\text{pos}},{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{M}}}_{t}^{\text{neg}}</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="alg3.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{A}_{\text{raw}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐀</mi><mtext>raw</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{A}_{\text{raw}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
             <span id="alg3.l3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each spatial query index <span id="alg3.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">q</span> <span id="alg3.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg3.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              <span id="alg3.l4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each prompt token index <span id="alg3.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_markedasmath ltx_font_typewriter">k</span> <span id="alg3.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="alg3.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
               <span id="alg3.l5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span> <math id="alg3.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{k}\in\tau_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">k</mtext><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{k}\in\tau_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">then</span>



</div>
<div id="alg3.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
                <math id="alg3.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{R}}}_{t}[\texttt{q},\texttt{k}]\leftarrow\cos({\boldsymbol{\mathbf{Q}}}_{t}[\texttt{q}],{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{e}}}_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">q</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">k</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>cos</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐐</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">q</mtext><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{R}}}_{t}[\texttt{q},\texttt{k}]\leftarrow\cos({\boldsymbol{\mathbf{Q}}}_{t}[\texttt{q}],{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{e}}}_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;">// Fairness match
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
               <span id="alg3.l7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">else</span>


</div>
<div id="alg3.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
                <math id="alg3.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{R}}}_{t}[\texttt{q},\texttt{k}]\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">q</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">k</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{R}}}_{t}[\texttt{q},\texttt{k}]\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
               <span id="alg3.l9.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">if</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              <span id="alg3.l10.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">11:</span>
              
             <span id="alg3.l11.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">12:</span>
              
             <math id="alg3.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{M}}}_{t}^{\text{fair}}\leftarrow{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{R}}}_{t}\odot{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{M}}}_{t}^{\text{pos}}-(1-{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{R}}}_{t})\odot{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{M}}}_{t}^{\text{neg}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>fair</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>pos</mtext></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>𝐑</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⊙</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐌</mi><mi>t</mi><mtext>neg</mtext></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{M}}}_{t}^{\text{fair}}\leftarrow{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{R}}}_{t}\odot{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{M}}}_{t}^{\text{pos}}-(1-{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{R}}}_{t})\odot{\boldsymbol{\mathbf{M}}}_{t}^{\text{neg}}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
